                <pb facs="0434" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg428"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No.
                    91.—Translation.—Personal.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Moret to Mr. Taylor.</hi></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Distinguished Friend</hi>: I have received your
                    note, and I confess that only your kindness may excuse my delay in fulfilling
                    the word which more than a month ago I gave you. Pardon me, however, in view of
                    my many occupations, all of an urgent character, which absorb all the time
                    necessary to discuss matters of such complication and delicacy as will occupy
                    us, in reference to the Mora claim. Wishing, however, to please you, and in
                    spite of it now being Christmas week, I purpose to call you on Wednesday, as on
                    Thursday there will be a council of ministers.</p>
                <p>With this motive, I am, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Moret.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
